---
/**
 * AB-RF1 · FILL
 *
 * ONE OF FOUR OPTIONS FOR THE REFUSAL — ab-rf1..rf4. The refusal is what the
 * send block says when it is pressed on an incomplete form: "Name and email
 * required". Nothing live is touched.
 *
 * ONLY THE REFUSAL DIFFERS ACROSS THESE FOUR. The waking of the action is
 * deliberately the same quiet 200ms fade-and-lift in all of them, so that
 * nothing competes with the thing being judged. ab-rf1..se4 are where the
 * WAKE was the subject; these four leave it alone.
 *
 * WHAT IS ALREADY TAKEN, and why none of these repeats it:
 *   the live block  send-swell — the characters thicken 400 to 700 and back
 *                   on a 25ms stagger, 1095ms end to end for twenty-three
 *                   characters. Slow enough to have stopped reading it.
 *   ab-rf1          the note arrives whole and a rule is struck under it
 *   ab-se2          weight and tracking spread, the mirror of the action
 *   ab-se3          the note is drawn out of the margin under a clip
 *   ab-se4          the arrow recoils and the note takes the shove
 *
 * SO THESE FOUR GO ELSEWHERE: a ground rather than the type, the words that
 * are actually missing, a caret, and the word as the unit rather than the
 * character. All four finish under 260ms.
 *
 * THE STATES ARE THE SITE'S OWN: .is-asking on the shell is the refusal, and
 * the script adds it on a click while the form is invalid.

 * ── THIS ONE: FILL ──────────────────────────────────────────────
 *
 * THE GROUND ANSWERS, NOT THE TYPE. Every refusal in the library so far does
 * something to the letters — thickens them, shoves them, draws them out of a
 * margin. This one does not touch them at all. A solid block of the accent
 * sweeps in behind the sentence, left to right, in 130ms; the letters knock
 * out of it to the page's own ground colour for as long as it is there; and
 * then the block drains away to the right over 110ms, leaving the words lit
 * in bone.
 *
 * IT IS A HIGHLIGHT USED AS AN ALARM, which is a piece of vocabulary the
 * page has not spent: a selection, a found term, a marked passage. It reads
 * as the interface pointing at the sentence rather than as the sentence
 * reacting.
 *
 * THE KNOCK-OUT IS WHAT MAKES IT WORK. A block sliding behind unchanged grey
 * type is a decoration. Flipping the letters to --ground for the 130ms the
 * block covers them means the sentence is genuinely inverted, and the eye
 * reads inversion far faster than it reads a colour change.
 *
 * IN AND OUT FROM OPPOSITE EDGES. The block enters scaling from the left and
 * leaves scaling to the right — one continuous sweep through the words
 * rather than a thing that arrives and then retreats the way it came. 240ms
 * for the whole pass.
 *
 * <- IT IS DRAWN BEHIND, WHICH TAKES ONE DECLARATION AND IS EASY TO GET
 *   WRONG. The block is a ::before on the note with z-index: -1 and the note
 *   itself gains no stacking context of its own, so the pseudo-element sits
 *   under the text rather than over it. Give .send__note a position and a
 *   z-index of its own and the block covers the words instead.
 */
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
const SEND = 'Send this enquiry';
const REFUSE = 'Name and email required';
---

<Base title="Fill — send block draft" description="An isolated draft of the send block's animation.">
  <main class="lab">
      <nav class="sw" aria-label="Variation">
        <span class="sw__t">Refusal · Fill</span>
        <a class="sw__i is-here" href="/preview/ab-rf1">RF1</a>
        <a class="sw__i" href="/preview/ab-rf2">RF2</a>
        <a class="sw__i" href="/preview/ab-rf3">RF3</a>
        <a class="sw__i" href="/preview/ab-rf4">RF4</a>
        <a class="sw__i sw__i--src" href="/preview/ab-rf1">SE1-4</a>
      </nav>

    <div class="lab__head">
      <p class="lab__k">ab-rf1 · Fill</p>
      <p class="lab__d">The ground answers, not the type. A solid accent block sweeps behind the words in 130ms and the letters knock out of it; the block then drains and leaves them lit.</p>
    </div>

    {/* The send block, markup faithful to ContactForm.astro: the sentence is
        written once for assistive tech and once as letters, and the letters
        are hidden from it. */}
    <div class="send" data-send>
      <div class="send__band">
        <a class="send__act" id="send" href="#" aria-disabled="true">
          <span class="visually-hidden">{SEND}</span>
          <span class="send__chars" aria-hidden="true">{SEND.split('').map((c, i) => (
            <i style={`--i:${i}`}>{c === ' ' ? '\u00A0' : c}</i>
          ))}</span>
          <span class="send__arrow" aria-hidden="true">→</span>
        </a>
        <p class="mono send__note" id="note"></p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="lab__ctl">
      <button type="button" data-act="wake">Wake the action</button>
      <button type="button" data-act="refuse">Refuse</button>
      <button type="button" data-act="ready">Ready note</button>
      <button type="button" data-act="reset">Reset</button>
      <span class="lab__state" data-state></span>
    </div>
  </main>
</Base>

<script is:inline define:vars={{ REFUSE }}>
  (function () {
    const shell = document.querySelector('[data-send]');
    const act = document.getElementById('send');
    const note = document.getElementById('note');
    const state = document.querySelector('[data-state]');
    const READY = 'Opens as a draft. Send it when you\u2019re ready.';

    /* ASTRO SCOPES THIS PAGE'S CSS BY STAMPING data-astro-cid-* ON EVERY
       ELEMENT IN THE TEMPLATE, and compiling `.send__ink` to
       `.send__ink[data-astro-cid-…]`. The note's characters are built here,
       so they are not in the template and never get stamped — and every
       rule below that targets .send__ink or .send__ink i would silently
       fail to match. Measured before this was added: the refusal ran its
       animation on nothing and the note stayed --dim.

       ContactForm.astro solves it the same way. Copying the attribute off
       the note itself keeps the stylesheet ordinary: no :global, no inline
       styles. (HANDOFF §6.) */
    const scope = Array.from(note.attributes).map((a) => a.name)
      .find((n) => n.startsWith('data-astro-cid-'));
    const stamp = (el) => { if (scope) el.setAttribute(scope, ''); return el; };

    /* The same split ContactForm's setNote() uses: one span for a screen
       reader, one per character for the ink. */
    function setNote(text) {
      note.textContent = '';
      const said = stamp(document.createElement('span'));
      said.className = 'visually-hidden';
      said.textContent = text;
      const ink = stamp(document.createElement('span'));
      ink.className = 'send__ink';
      ink.setAttribute('aria-hidden', 'true');
      for (let i = 0; i < text.length; i++) {
        const ch = stamp(document.createElement('i'));
        ch.style.setProperty('--i', String(i));
        ch.textContent = text[i];
        ink.appendChild(ch);
      }
      note.append(said, ink);
    }

    function say(s) { state.textContent = s; }

    function reset() {
      act.classList.remove('is-ready', 'is-woken');
      shell.classList.remove('is-asking');
      act.setAttribute('aria-disabled', 'true');
      setNote(REFUSE);
      say('idle — not ready');
    }

    /* Re-adding a class does not restart an animation unless the element is
       reflowed in between. */
    function restart(el, cls) {
      el.classList.remove(cls);
      void el.offsetWidth;
      el.classList.add(cls);
    }

    document.querySelector('.lab__ctl').addEventListener('click', (e) => {
      const b = e.target.closest('[data-act]');
      if (!b) return;
      const a = b.dataset.act;
      if (a === 'reset') return reset();
      if (a === 'wake') {
        act.classList.add('is-ready');
        act.setAttribute('aria-disabled', 'false');
        shell.classList.remove('is-asking');
        setNote(READY);
        restart(act, 'is-woken');
        say('woken — ready');
      }
      if (a === 'refuse') {
        act.classList.remove('is-ready', 'is-woken');
        act.setAttribute('aria-disabled', 'true');
        setNote(REFUSE);
        restart(shell, 'is-asking');
        say('refused');
      }
      if (a === 'ready') { setNote(READY); say('ready note'); }
    });

    act.addEventListener('click', (e) => {
      e.preventDefault();
      if (!act.classList.contains('is-ready')) {
        setNote(REFUSE);
        restart(shell, 'is-asking');
        say('refused');
      }
    });

    reset();
  })();
</script>

<style>
  /* ══ THE HARNESS ═════════════════════════════════════════════════
     Not design. Enough page to judge the block on, and controls to replay
     the states without filling a form at the bottom of a 15,000px page. */
  .lab {
    min-height: 100vh; padding: clamp(28px, 7vh, 80px) var(--margin);
    display: flex; flex-direction: column; justify-content: center; gap: 44px;
    max-width: 980px;
  }
  .lab__k {
    margin: 0 0 8px; font-family: var(--mono); font-size: var(--t-micro);
    letter-spacing: 0.16em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--accent);
  }
  .lab__d { margin: 0; max-width: 62ch; color: var(--muted); font-size: var(--t-sm); line-height: 1.5; }
  .lab__ctl { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 10px; align-items: center; }
  .lab__ctl button {
    font-family: var(--mono); font-size: 11px; letter-spacing: 0.12em;
    text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--muted);
    background: transparent; border: 1px solid var(--rule);
    padding: 9px 14px; border-radius: 999px; cursor: pointer;
    transition: color 140ms linear, border-color 140ms linear;
  }
  .lab__ctl button:hover { color: var(--bone); border-color: var(--bone-dim); }
  .lab__state {
    font-family: var(--mono); font-size: 11px; letter-spacing: 0.12em;
    text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--dim); margin-left: 6px;
  }
  .sw {
    position: fixed; top: 14px; right: 16px; z-index: 40;
    display: flex; align-items: baseline; gap: 12px;
    font-family: var(--mono); font-size: var(--t-micro);
    letter-spacing: 0.16em; text-transform: uppercase;
  }
  .sw__t { color: var(--muted); }
  .sw a { color: var(--dim); text-decoration: none; transition: color 140ms linear; }
  .sw a:hover { color: var(--bone); }
  .sw a.is-here { color: var(--accent); }
  .sw a.sw__i--src { color: var(--muted); margin-left: 5px; }

  /* ══ THE BLOCK, AS THE SITE HAS IT ═══════════════════════════════
     Structure and type copied from ContactForm.astro so the draft is judged
     at the real size and in the real layout. Everything the VARIATION
     changes is in the block below this one. */
  .send__band {
    display: flex; align-items: baseline; gap: var(--s-2); flex-wrap: wrap;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--rule); padding-top: 26px;
  }
  .send__act {
    font-family: var(--display); font-weight: 500;
    font-size: clamp(1.75rem, 3.06vw, 2.75rem);
    letter-spacing: -0.035em; line-height: 1;
    color: var(--bone); text-decoration: none; white-space: nowrap;
    display: inline-flex; align-items: baseline; gap: 0.3em;
    cursor: not-allowed;
  }
  .send__act.is-ready { cursor: pointer; }
  .send__chars i, .send__ink i { display: inline-block; font-style: normal; }
  .send__arrow { display: inline-block; }
  .send__note {
    margin: 0 0 0 auto; text-align: right;
    color: var(--dim); font-size: 14px; line-height: 1.8; max-width: 32ch;
  }
  .send__ink { display: inline-block; white-space: pre-wrap; transform-origin: right center; }
  @media (max-width: 620px) {
    .send__band { flex-direction: column; gap: 18px; }
    .send__note { margin-left: 0; text-align: left; }
    .send__ink { transform-origin: left center; }
    .send__act { white-space: normal; }
  }

  /* ══ THE WAKE, IDENTICAL IN ALL FOUR ═════════════════════════════
     Quiet on purpose. The refusal is what is being judged here, so the
     action's arrival is a 200ms fade and a 0.06em lift with a 6ms stagger —
     present, over before it is noticed, and the same in rf1..rf4. */
  .send__chars i { opacity: 0.32; transform: translateY(0.06em); }
  .send__act.is-woken .send__chars i {
    animation: rf-wake 200ms cubic-bezier(0.2, 0.9, 0.2, 1) both;
    animation-delay: calc(var(--i) * 6ms);
  }
  @keyframes rf-wake {
    from { opacity: 0.32; transform: translateY(0.06em); }
    to   { opacity: 1; transform: none; }
  }
  .send__arrow { opacity: 0.32; }
  .send__act.is-woken .send__arrow { opacity: 1; transition: opacity 200ms linear 110ms; }
  .send__act.is-ready:hover { color: var(--accent); }
  .send__act.is-ready:hover .send__arrow { transform: translateX(0.28em); transition: transform 140ms cubic-bezier(0.2, 0.9, 0.2, 1); }
  .send.is-asking .send__act { color: var(--dim); }

  /* ══ RF1 · FILL ══════════════════════════════════════════════════ */
  .send__note { position: relative; }
  .send__ink { position: relative; }
  .send__ink::before {
    content: ''; position: absolute; z-index: -1;
    left: -0.35em; right: -0.35em; top: -0.15em; bottom: -0.1em;
    background: var(--accent);
    transform: scaleX(0); transform-origin: left center;
  }
  .send.is-asking .send__ink::before {
    animation: rf1-sweep 240ms cubic-bezier(0.3, 0.8, 0.3, 1) both;
  }
  @keyframes rf1-sweep {
    0%   { transform: scaleX(0); transform-origin: left center; }
    54%  { transform: scaleX(1); transform-origin: left center; }
    55%  { transform: scaleX(1); transform-origin: right center; }
    100% { transform: scaleX(0); transform-origin: right center; }
  }
  /* Knocked out while the block is over them, lit after it has gone. */
  .send.is-asking .send__ink { animation: rf1-knock 240ms linear both; }
  @keyframes rf1-knock {
    0%, 4%   { color: var(--dim); }
    5%, 50%  { color: var(--ground); }
    62%, 100% { color: var(--bone); }
  }

  @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
    .send.is-asking .send__ink::before { animation: none; transform: scaleX(0); }
    .send.is-asking .send__ink { animation: none; color: var(--bone); }
  }
</style>
